              "id": "1773685546464_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT:\n {{$context.$nodes.ASSIGN_NEXT_BEST_ACTIONS_TO_CUSTOMERS.$output.result}} \nTASK:\nGenerate output EXACTLY in the required <oraInsight> format.\nPROCESSING RULES:\n1. FILTERING:\n- Process ONLY those records where:\n  - \"primaryActions\" exists AND is a non-empty array\n- COMPLETELY IGNORE the \"priority\" field from input data\n- Do NOT filter based on HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW / Requires Review\n2. OUTPUT GENERATION:\n- For EACH record that passes the filter:\n  - For EACH item in \"primaryActions\":\n    - Generate ONE <oraInsight> block\n    - Determine action type using primaryActions[].code:\n      - If primaryActions[].code = \"emailActions\", use EMAIL ACTION MAPPING\n      - Otherwise, use STANDARD ACTION MAPPING\n3. FIELD MAPPING:\nA. STANDARD ACTION MAPPING\nUse this mapping when primaryActions[].code is NOT \"emailActions\".\n- title:\n  EXACT value from:\n  primaryActions[].action\n- actionText:\n  EXACT value from:\n  primaryActions[].action\n- shortDescription:\n  MUST be LLM generated:\n  - Single sentence\n  - Maximum 20 words\n  - MUST include:\n    - customerName\n    - accountNumber\n    - reason derived from matchedConditions (e.g., high balance, overdue invoices, etc.)\n    - urgency (why action is needed now)\n    - If the response includes customerName, display the values directly without prefixing them with words such as customer.\n  - Do NOT repeat action text verbatim\n- followUpCommand:\n  MUST be constructed EXACTLY as:\n  ora.Agent(<command>,<FULL_CUSTOMER_JSON_RECORD>)\n  Where:\n  - <command> = EXACT value from primaryActions[].command\n  - <command> MUST be a bare identifier and NOT quoted\n  - <FULL_CUSTOMER_JSON_RECORD> = ENTIRE original customer object\n  - DO NOT modify, remove, rename, reorder, or summarize ANY fields\n  - Preserve ALL nested arrays and objects EXACTLY\n- priority:\n  ALWAYS true (hardcoded, NOT derived from input)\nB. EMAIL ACTION MAPPING\nUse this mapping only when primaryActions[].code = \"emailActions\".\n- title:\n  EXACT value from:\n  primaryActions[].title\n- actionText:\n  EXACT value from:\n  primaryActions[].actionText\n- shortDescription:\n  MUST be LLM generated:\n  - Single sentence\n  - Maximum 20 words\n  - MUST include:\n    - customerName from primaryActions[].additionalContext.customerName\n    - accountNumber from primaryActions[].additionalContext.accountNumber\n    - intentMeaning from primaryActions[].additionalContext.intentMeaning\n    - Must use primaryActions[].shortDescription with key details such as amounts, invoice count as supporting details\n    - If the response includes customerName, display the values directly without prefixing them with words such as customer.\n- followUpPayload: primaryActions[].followUpPayload\n- followUpCommand:\n  MUST be constructed EXACTLY as:\n  ora.Agent(emailActions,<followUpPayload>)\n  Where:\n  - emailActions MUST be a bare identifier and NOT quoted\n  - <followUpPayload> = EXACT value from primaryActions[].followUpPayload\n  - DO NOT pass the full customer JSON record\n  - Preserve ALL nested arrays and objects EXACTLY\n- priority:\n  ALWAYS true (hardcoded, NOT derived from input)\n4. STRICT OUTPUT FORMAT:\n- Output ONLY <oraInsight> blocks\n- NO extra text before or after\n- NO explanations\n- NO markdown\n- NO JSON array wrapper\nEach block MUST follow EXACT structure:\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"...\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"...\",\n  \"actionText\": \"...\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Agent(command,{FULL_JSON})\",\n  \"priority\": true\n}\n</oraInsight>\n5. CRITICAL VALIDATION RULES (MANDATORY):\n- DO NOT skip any record that has non-empty primaryActions\n- DO NOT use input \"priority\" field anywhere in logic\n- Determine mapping strictly by primaryActions[].code\n- If primaryActions[].code = \"emailActions\":\n  - MUST use EMAIL ACTION MAPPING only\n  - MUST NOT use primaryActions[].action or primaryActions[].command\n  - MUST NOT pass the full customer JSON record\n  - MUST pass primaryActions[].additionalContext as the second argument\n  - command inside ora.Agent MUST be bare emailActions and NOT quoted\n- If primaryActions[].code is NOT \"emailActions\":\n  - MUST use STANDARD ACTION MAPPING only\n  - MUST use primaryActions[].action and primaryActions[].command\n  - MUST pass the full customer JSON record as the second argument\n- DO NOT:\n  - Rename fields\n  - Modify JSON structure\n  - Escape or stringify JSON incorrectly\n  - Add/remove attributes\n  - Quote the command inside ora.Agent()\n- The command inside ora.Agent MUST be:\n  - a bare identifier, for example callCustomer or emailActions\n  - NOT a string, for example \"callCustomer\" or \"emailActions\"\n- If ANY rule is violated:\n  → REGENERATE the output\n6. OUTPUT COMPLETENESS:\n- If a record has N primaryActions:\n  → Generate N <oraInsight> blocks\n- Ensure ALL eligible records are processed\nFINAL INSTRUCTION:\nReturn ONLY valid <oraInsight> blocks exactly matching the required format.\nDO NOT include anything else."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Action Code",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let suggestedAction = String($context.$app.$OraAction || \"\").trim();\n\nif (!suggestedAction) {\n  throw new Error(\"OraAction is empty\");\n}\n\n// Case 1: oraFormSubmit → extract id\nlet match = suggestedAction.match(/^<oraFormSubmit\\b[^>]*id=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i);\nif (match) {\n  return match[1];\n}\n\n// Case 2: ora.Agent(...)\nmatch = suggestedAction.match(/^ora\\.Agent\\(\\s*\"?([A-Za-z0-9_]+)\"?\\s*,/i);\nif (match) {\n  return match[1];\n}\n\n// Case 3: plain action with comma payload\nmatch = suggestedAction.match(/^\"?([A-Za-z0-9_]+)\"?\\s*,/);\nif (match) {\n  return match[1];\n}\n\n// Case 4: simple string\nmatch = suggestedAction.match(/^\"?([A-Za-z0-9_]+)\"?$/);\nif (match) {\n  return match[1];\n}\n\nthrow new Error(\"Unable to extract action code from OraAction: \" + suggestedAction);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775075446144"
          },
          "diagram": {
