          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_UNAUTHORIZED_COLLECTOR_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1780310215180",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780310215180_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise application.\n\nContext:\n- The current user attempted to perform an action that requires the Collector responsibility.\n- The system has determined that the current user is not assigned the Collector responsibility.\n- This is an authorization/access issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message telling the user that they cannot continue because they are not assigned the Collector responsibility.\n\nRules:\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, SQL, APIs, tools, roles tables, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not suggest retrying the same action.\n4. Do not blame the user.\n5. Do not invent any additional responsibilities or access details.\n6. Tell the user to contact their administrator if they need access.\n7. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n- The user is not assigned the Collector responsibility.\n- The requested action cannot be completed without that responsibility.\n- The user should contact their administrator to request access.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output:\nYou are not assigned the Collector responsibility required to perform this action. Please contact your administrator if you need access."
            },
            {
              "id": "1780310215180_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Display error message for Collector retrieval",
            "name": "Display Error Message for Collector Retrieval"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7835.5,
            "y": 8092
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_MESSAGE_FOR_COLLECTOR_RETRIEVAL",
          "id": "1780690564543",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780690564543_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise agentic application.\n\nContext:\n- The current user attempted to access the Collector Workspace Agentic Application.\n- The access attempt returned this error information:\n  {{$context.$nodes.GET_COLLECTOR_ID.$error.$info}}\n- If the error information contains status 5XX, treat it as Read Only Data Store not being enabled.\n- If the error information contains status 403, treat it as the user not having permission to access the agent.\n- This is either a configuration prerequisite issue or an access permission issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message explaining why the user cannot access the Collector Workspace Agentic Application.\n\nRules:\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, SQL, APIs, tools, services, status codes, error objects, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not suggest retrying the same action before the required configuration or access change is completed.\n4. Do not blame the user.\n5. Do not invent any additional setup steps, permissions, roles, or configuration details.\n6. If the error information indicates status 500, tell the user that Read Only Data Store must be configured before accessing the Collector Workspace Agentic Application.\n7. If the error information indicates status 403, tell the user that they do not have permission to access the Collector Workspace Agentic Application and should contact their administrator if they need access.\n8. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n- For status 500: Read Only Data Store is not enabled, and the application cannot be accessed until it is configured.\n- For status 403: The user does not have permission to access the Collector Workspace Agentic Application, and should contact their administrator if they need access.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output for status 500:\nRead Only Data Store is not enabled. Please configure Read Only Data Store before accessing the Collector Workspace Agentic Application.\n\nExample output for status 403:\nYou do not have permission to access the Collector Workspace Agentic Application. Please contact your administrator if you need access."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
