        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Flatten Aging Buckets",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const data = $context.$nodes.AGING_BUCKETS_EXTRACT.$output || [];\n\nconst result = {};\n\ndata.forEach(row => {\n  const name = row.CUSTOMERNAME;\n  const bucketKey = `AGINGBUCKETS ${row.DAYSLATE} ${row.INVOICEREMAININGAMOUNTCURRENCY}`;\n  const amountKey = bucketKey + \" AMOUNT\";\n  const currencyKey = bucketKey + \" CURRENCY\";\n\n  if (!result[name]) {\n    result[name] = {\n      CUSTOMERNAME: name,\n      CUSTOMERACCOUNTID: row.CUSTOMERACCOUNTID\n    };\n  }\n\n  result[name][amountKey] = (result[name][amountKey] || 0) + row.INVOICEREMAININGAMOUNT;\n  result[name][currencyKey] = row.INVOICEREMAININGAMOUNTCURRENCY;\n});\n\nreturn Object.values(result);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780523183558"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6748.922174223036,
            "y": 7803.572563083888
          },
          "code": "FLATTEN_AGING_BUCKETS",
          "id": "1773351694810",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Error Message for Policy Document"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9607,
            "y": 5000
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_MESSAGE_FOR_POLICY_DOCUMENT",
          "id": "1780612415695",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780612415695_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1780612415695_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise application.\n\nContext:\n\n* The current user attempted to extract and process a Policy document.\n* The system has determined that the document cannot be processed because it is not a valid Policy document or does not meet the requirements for Policy document processing.\n* This is a document validation issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message telling the user that the document cannot be processed.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, AI models, extraction services, APIs, tools, validation rules, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not suggest retrying the same action with the same document.\n4. Do not blame the user.\n5. Do not invent additional document requirements.\n6. Tell the user to verify that the correct Policy document has been provided.\n7. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n\n* The submitted document cannot be processed as a Policy document.\n* The requested extraction and processing cannot be completed.\n* The user should verify that they have provided the correct Policy document.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output:\nThe document provided cannot be processed as a Policy document. Please verify that you have selected the correct Policy document and try again."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Error Message for FX Currency Conversion"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 10136,
            "y": 5000
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_MESSAGE_FOR_FX_CURRENCY_CONVERSION",
          "id": "1780612612159",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780612612159_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise application.\n\nContext:\n\n* The current user attempted to perform a Foreign Exchange (FX) currency conversion as part of a business process.\n* The system was unable to determine a valid exchange rate for the requested currency conversion.\n* This is a data availability issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message telling the user that the currency conversion cannot be completed.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, APIs, exchange rate providers, services, tools, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not blame the user.\n4. Do not invent reasons for the unavailable exchange rate.\n5. Do not suggest technical troubleshooting steps.\n6. Tell the user to contact their administrator if they need assistance.\n7. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n\n* The requested currency conversion cannot be completed because a valid exchange rate is not available.\n* The requested processing cannot continue without the exchange rate.\n* The user should contact their administrator for assistance.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output:\nThe requested currency conversion cannot be completed because a valid exchange rate is not available. Please contact your administrator if you need assistance."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Error Message for Multi Currency Failure"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 10728,
            "y": 5000
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_MESSAGE_FOR_MULTI_CURRENCY_FAILURE",
          "id": "1780612724388",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780612724388_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise application.\n\nContext:\n\n* The current user attempted to process a transaction involving multiple currencies.\n* The system has determined that the transaction cannot be processed because multiple currencies are present and the required currency handling cannot be completed.\n* This is a business processing issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message telling the user that the transaction cannot continue.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, APIs, tools, currency conversion services, exchange rate calculations, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not blame the user.\n4. Do not invent additional currency requirements or processing rules.\n5. Do not suggest technical troubleshooting steps.\n6. Tell the user to contact their administrator if they need assistance.\n7. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n\n* The transaction contains multiple currencies and cannot be processed as submitted.\n* The requested processing cannot be completed.\n* The user should contact their administrator for assistance.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output:\nThe transaction contains multiple currencies and cannot be processed as submitted. Please contact your administrator if you need assistance."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Error Message for Final Customer Data Failure"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11320,
            "y": 5000
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_MESSAGE_FOR_FINAL_CUSTOMER_DATA_FAILURE",
          "id": "1780612841595",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780612841595_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a final user-facing message for an enterprise application.\n\nContext:\n\n* The current user attempted to prioritize customers and assign Next Best Actions (NBAs).\n* The system was unable to determine a valid prioritization or generate Next Best Actions for one or more customers.\n* This is a business data or eligibility issue, not a technical failure.\n\nInstruction:\nGenerate a clear, polite, and concise message telling the user that prioritization and Next Best Action assignment cannot be completed.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Do not mention internal checks, backend logic, scoring models, AI models, algorithms, APIs, tools, ranking calculations, or implementation details.\n2. Do not say the system failed.\n3. Do not blame the user.\n4. Do not invent specific eligibility criteria, prioritization rules, or customer attributes.\n5. Do not suggest technical troubleshooting steps.\n6. Tell the user to review the customer data and contact their administrator if assistance is needed.\n7. Return only the final message to be displayed to the user.\n\nRequired message intent:\n\n* Customer prioritization and Next Best Action assignment could not be completed.\n* The requested processing cannot continue without sufficient information to determine recommendations.\n* The user should review the customer data and contact their administrator if assistance is needed.\n\nFinal output format:\nReturn one short paragraph only.\n\nExample output:\nCustomer prioritization and Next Best Action assignment could not be completed because sufficient information was not available to determine recommendations. Please review the customer data and contact your administrator if you need assistance."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
